From b078a7a7719076a2e1884bfe2bd993e76c078a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:59:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: verify synchronous broadcast scripts outside the chain
 lock

Concurrent sendrawtransaction clients previously serialized script checks
under cs_main even when peer admission used unlocked verification.

For synchronous broadcasts with -parallelmempool enabled, resolve inputs
with the same deferred PreChecks used by staged peer admission, copy the
spent outputs, release the locks and verify scripts on the calling RPC
thread. Advisory cache entries are uncached before unlocking. The original
locked BroadcastTransaction critical section still checks chain/mempool
presence, admits with current policy and fee bounds, marks unbroadcast
transactions and fences validation-interface callbacks before returning.
Only matching spent outputs, transaction ID and flags reuse script results.

Synchronous callers already promise they hold no chain/mempool/wallet
locks. Asynchronous callers retain their existing lock contract and
ordinary admission. -parallelmempool=0 selects the original serial path;
-parallelmempoolthreads controls P2P workers, while independent RPC request
threads do their own script work. Update option help to explain both paths.

Validation: assembled Chronik-enabled Release daemon/test/benchmark build
and 62 directly related native cases pass, including spent-output/flag
mismatch, cheap reject gating and validation-interface callback fencing.
Focused functional and RPC flood results are recorded in the delivery
README; full functional coverage and Linux validation remain separate.

How to reproduce:
    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 ninja -C build -j2 bitcoind test_bitcoin
    build/src/test/test_bitcoin \
        --run_test=mempool_admission_tests,validationinterface_tests
    contrib/bench/mempool-admission/ab.py \
        --bitcoind new=build/src/bitcoind \
        --config serial=new:-parallelmempool=0 \
        --config parallel=new:-parallelmempool=1 \
        --fixture FX --workdir AB-RPC --mode rpc --peers 8 --rounds 5
The driver prints medians/min-max for complete floods and retains failed
attempts, exact transaction coverage, node/fixture/tool hashes and settings.

